WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.990
- Thanks to Ron DeSantis,

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:01.890
the immigrants that he sent

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.730
to Martha's Vineyard

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.170
may be staying in the US for good.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.460
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.868
made headlines for chartering a flight

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.400
from Texas to Massachusetts

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.049
in order to dump 50 asylum seekers

00:00:10.049 --> 00:00:11.280
in Martha's Vineyard

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.390
as a political stunt.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.350
This may all have backfired

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.730
because the Bexar County Sheriff,

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.140
Javier Salazar, said that

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.220
the DeSantis migrants

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.300
were victims of a crime.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.590
People who are crime victims

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.940
or witnesses to a crime

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:22.710
are eligible for
something called a U Visa,

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.870
which allows them to remain in the US.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:25.958
Congress created the U Visa

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:27.690
with the passage of the victims

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.970
of Trafficking and
Violence Protection Act.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:30.090
Immigrants who are willing

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.320
to help law enforcement authorities

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.760
in the investigation or prosecution

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.840
of the criminal activity

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.520
could eventually get a green card.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.960
He signed the certification forms

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.793
for all the migrants

00:00:37.793 --> 00:00:39.030
saying that they were transported

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.050
under false pretenses,

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.010
which is the crime

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.420
of unlawful restraint.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.670
Under Texas Penal Code Section 20.02,

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.110
a person commits an offense

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.430
if he intentionally or knowingly

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:48.480
restrains another person.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.650
Unlawful restraint can be

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.700
a Class A Misdemeanor,

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.660
state jail felony,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.740
or third degree felony

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.219
depending on the nature of the offense.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:56.013
So way to go, Ron.

